ter the transfer of two North Korean POWs to South Korea. The South insists the move was to be kept secret as it seeks to avoid antagonizing Pyongyang.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition parties march to Supreme Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1ef4018bfd55a9552b169006c614fed9d157dd984494934cc4165f96faf8f60</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-parties-march-to-supreme-court/live-79638649--6608bc6a2872.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-parties-march-to-supreme-court/live-79638649?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Intensifying their demand for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation, opposition parties are holding a march to the Supreme Court. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires missiles after Seoul's hypersonic test</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60a3530a85cd94d8dde21803b5cc34e309c21ec44ffe750db46fd6607e2d1740</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T03:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-missiles-after-seoul-s-hypersonic-test/a-79636110--0922c7762fcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-missiles-after-seoul-s-hypersonic-test/a-79636110?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea has conducted its fourth missile launch in October. South Korea's military called this launch a "show of force" in response to South Korea's successful test launch of a hypersonic missile.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: President puts Khan stronghold province under emergency rule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d657de329865a1c57634f700a6636c165cec535f6aa53875045aa500a9b3ac2b</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-president-puts-khan-stronghold-province-under-emergency-rule/a-79632530--660fdc13d98b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-president-puts-khan-stronghold-province-under-emergency-rule/a-79632530?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Asif Ali Zardari has effectively suspended the provincial government in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa. The northwestern state is an epicenter of support for former PM Imran Khan and run by his PTI party.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is China seeking to restrict Taiwan's cultural presence?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:952b7f381d83cac7aa2b44a7247abd1ad5b995bdb1c84dc7e893a4ccb3e39158</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T06:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947--71784c91bb83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From coffee competitions to literature awards, Beijing appears to be working to limit Taiwan's international cultural and political impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3f0b02e37b702af046f0b2b434d0214372570718592d22912b045d54c91255</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:56:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--5ad51afec87b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-13T06:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
